IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 422 of 2014
CITATION: (2014) 10 SCC 473
YEAR: 2014

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: R.M. Lodha, Kurian Joseph, R.F. Nariman

PARTIES:
Anvar P.V. vs P.K. Basheer

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Indian Evidence Act, 1872

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 65B Evidence Act, Section 63 Evidence Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
electronic record admissibility, special law over general, cds and dvds, oral evidence barred

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Overruled Navjot Sandhu on electronic evidence, holding that Sections 65A and 65B constitute a complete code and electronic records cannot be proved by general oral evidence.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 65B Evidence Act, Section 63 Evidence Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

